statement:
Let $A,I,P_n=A/I^n$ be a coefficient datum as in [def-weil-pbc-complete-coefficient-datum] and let $f:X\to Y$ be a morphism of schemes. For $W=X,Y$ use the small pro-etale site, the constant ring sheaves $\underline A_W,\underline{P_n}_W$, module sheaves and the ordinary unbounded derived category $D(W,A)$ [def-weil-pbc-proetale-site, def-weil-pbc-constant-sheaf, def-weil-sheaf-of-modules-category, def-weil-abstract-derived-category], with K-injective derived direct image $Rf_*$ [def-pur-kinjective-complex]. Put $\mathcal T_W=\operatorname{Fun}(\mathbf N_{\geq1}^{op},\operatorname{Mod}(\underline A_W))$ [def-weil-inverse-system], realized as modules on the diagram site [lem-weil-pbc-diagram-site-realization], with constant-tower functor $\Delta$, evaluations $\operatorname{ev}_n$, total derived inverse limit $\mathcal L_W=R\lim$ [lem-weil-pbc-ringed-strict-tower-homotopy-limit], and $R_f^{\mathcal T}:D(\mathcal T_X)\to D(\mathcal T_Y)$ the total right derived functor of termwise direct image (the direct image of the induced morphism of diagram ringed topoi). Let $\mathcal R_W(M)=\Delta M\otimes^L_{\Delta\underline A_W}(\underline{P_n}_W)_n$ and let $i_M:\Delta M\to\mathcal R_W(M)$ be the tensor of $\Delta M$ with the strict quotient map $\Delta\underline A_W\to(\underline{P_n}_W)_n$. Let $a_{f,N}:Rf_*\mathcal L_X(N)\xrightarrow{\sim}\mathcal L_Y(R_f^{\mathcal T}N)$ be the canonical comparison of [lem-weil-ringed-tower-pushforward-limit-comparison], with its evaluation identifications $\operatorname{ev}_nR_f^{\mathcal T}N\cong Rf_*\operatorname{ev}_nN$.

Then for every $M\in D(X,A)$:
(1) there is a canonical natural isomorphism $\chi_{f,M}:\Delta(Rf_*M)\xrightarrow{\sim}R_f^{\mathcal T}(\Delta M)$, represented for a K-injective representative $J$ of $M$ by the equality $f_*\Delta J=\Delta f_*J$;
(2) under the evaluation identifications, $\operatorname{ev}_n(\chi_{f,M})$ is the identity of $Rf_*M$ for every $n$;
(3) with the canonical identifications $\mathcal L_X(\Delta M)\cong M$ and $\mathcal L_Y(\Delta Rf_*M)\cong Rf_*M$, the composite $\mathcal L_Y(\chi_{f,M})^{-1}\circ a_{f,\Delta M}$ is the identity of $Rf_*M$;
(4) let $h_{f,M}:\mathcal R_Y(Rf_*M)\to R_f^{\mathcal T}\mathcal R_X(M)$ be the projection-formula map of [lem-weil-pbc-ringed-projection-mate-exact] on the diagram sites, for the object $\Delta M$ and the coefficient tower $(\underline{P_n}_Y)_n$, with its source identified through $\chi_{f,M}$; then
$$h_{f,M}\circ i_{Rf_*M}=R_f^{\mathcal T}(i_M)\circ\chi_{f,M}$$
in $D(\mathcal T_Y)$.
